          "timeout": 10,
          "statusMessage": "Lean detected \u2014 recalling the Vox loop"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "hooks": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "jq -r '.tool_input.file_path // empty' | grep -q '[.]lean$' && printf '%s' '{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"additionalContext\":\"LEAN PROOF LOOP \u2014 do not hand-debug tactics.\\n1. In Lean: #lift <theorem> emits the structure word.\\n2. vox verdict <word> reads it: T closes, B locates the arm left OPEN, N never forked, F is ill-typed. B tells you WHERE the proof is open, which a Lean error message does not.\\n3. python3 ~/imsgct/p4rakernel/scan_banked_counts.py finds a count carried in the open through a reversal \u2014 the repair is to bank it (open the region that HOLDS the result before the one that COMPUTES it), not to patch the tactic.\\n4. Walk it: ./run_hosted.sh then erdos <name> \u2014 the kernel computes the claim instead of printing it.\\nReach for these before iterating on error messages.\"}}' || true",
          "timeout": 10,
          "statusMessage": "Lean file \u2014 recalling the Vox loop"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "matcher": "Bash",
      "hooks": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "jq -r '.tool_input.command // empty' | grep -qE '(^| |/)vox |(^| )imasm |(^| )imscribe |cl8nk|cl9nk|run_hosted_cmds|decompose' && printf '%s' '{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"PreToolUse\", \"additionalContext\": \"IMASM / VOX \u2014 the traps, before you read a number.\\n1. THE VERB MAKES THE GRAPH. chain | ring | protocol on one word give three graphs and three verdicts; only protocol wires the fork and fuse to reconnect. A verdict is never a property of the glyph string alone.\\n2. PAIRING IS ANCESTRY, over edges, never text position. A fuse pairs with the innermost fork all its in-arms trace back to.\\n3. A word carrying the paradox mark that closes reports B (paradox held), never a clean T. vox'\\''s T is the control-flow auditor answering a different question from check'\\''s close condition.\\n4. ROTAT ON ONE RING IS A SYMMETRY and changes nothing measurable. A landing that varies with the cut is measuring the cut. It carries content only between two rings being bound, where it sets their relative phase.\\n5. VOX NEEDS A REAL ARTIFACT. Handed source it disassembles UTF-8 as x86 and still prints verdicts. Its first line says raw or elf \u2014 read that word before any number.\\n6. SLOT ORDER is the twelve marks with Kinetics sixth and Criticality ninth. The Imscriber'\\''s Guide Part I transposes those two; the tool wins.\\nRun the control before a measurement is a finding: shuffle the input and measure again. Full rules: ig-docs/IMSCRIBERS_GUIDE_TO_IMASM.md, or `imasm ref` for the live ones.\"}}' || true",
          "timeout": 10,
          "statusMessage": "Grammar instrument \u2014 recalling the traps"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "Stop": [
    {
      "matcher": "*",
      "hooks": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "python3 ~/.claude/hooks/output_guard.py",
          "timeout": 15,
          "statusMessage": "checking what I just said"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "UserPromptSubmit": [
    {
      "matcher": "*",
      "hooks": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "python3 ~/.claude/hooks/rider.py",
          "timeout": 10,
          "statusMessage": "the rider"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

